`embInfFun` sends an element of stage \(n\) to the thread whose coordinates climb from that element when the stage is later and descend when it is earlier. `embInfFun_coe` is that equality by definition. `embInf_monotone` compares the threads coordinatewise, and each coordinate of the climbing-and-descending sequence is monotone. `embInf_preservesDirectedSup` says the bare embedding preserves directed suprema: the image of a nonempty directed set is nonempty and directed because the embedding is monotone, and at each coordinate the supremum is the supremum of the corresponding components, which preserve it.
